  "statement_token": "\"Let $n$ be a positive integer, let a standardized Laplacian matrix of order $n$ be a matrix of the type considered in the paper, and let $S$ be the polygon defined earlier as the region containing the spectra of these matrices. **Spectrum-polygon conjecture.** The set of all eigenvalues of standardized Laplacian matrices of order $n$ coincides with $S$. The preceding theorem proves that every point of $S$ is an eigenvalue of some standardized Laplacian matrix of order $n$; the conjecture asserts the converse inclusion as well. The claim is presented as unproved in the source.\"",
